{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#471","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#471","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#471\",\"parent_revision\":\"06fbed04ab7c3cbce52e79cee3c5a655e7fc9ad7dbcb283ddfb81c9cb76c69be\",\"root_revision\":\"06fbed04ab7c3cbce52e79cee3c5a655e7fc9ad7dbcb283ddfb81c9cb76c69be\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nNo tool in backlog_core/server.py uses `tags=`. FastMCP v3 tag-based filtering allows servers (or composed parent servers) to expose only subsets of tools based on client role or context.\\n\\nFor backlog_core this has a practical use: when mounted into a larger MCP server (e.g., a project orchestrator), the parent could use `include_tags={\\\"read-only\\\"}` to expose only list/view tools to read-only clients, or `exclude_tags={\\\"destructive\\\"}` to prevent accidental closes/resolves.\\n\\nProposed tag assignments:\\n- `{\\\"read-only\\\"}` \u2192 backlog_list, backlog_view\\n- `{\\\"write\\\", \\\"github\\\"}` \u2192 backlog_add, backlog_update, backlog_groom, backlog_sync, backlog_pull\\n- `{\\\"destructive\\\", \\\"github\\\"}` \u2192 backlog_close, backlog_resolve\\n- `{\\\"maintenance\\\"}` \u2192 backlog_normalize\\n\\nFiles affected: `.claude/skills/backlog/backlog_core/server.py`\\n\\nSource: FastMCP v3 docs `servers/server.mdx` \u2014 `tags=` on decorators; `include_tags`/`exclude_tags` on `FastMCP()` constructor; `mcp.disable(tags={...})` at runtime.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | FastMCP v3 `tags=` on decorators verified | AVAILABLE | Item description cites `servers/server.mdx` |\\n| 2 | All tool definitions in server.py | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` |\\n| 3 | FastMCP version in use supports tags | DERIVABLE | Check pyproject.toml |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 straightforward mechanical change.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Trivial mechanical change. Additive metadata only. Zero risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `backlog_list` and `backlog_view` tagged `{'read-only'}`\\n- `backlog_add`, `backlog_update`, `backlog_groom`, `backlog_sync`, `backlog_pull` tagged `{'write', 'github'}`\\n- `backlog_close` and `backlog_resolve` tagged `{'destructive', 'github'}`\\n- `backlog_normalize` tagged `{'maintenance'}`\\n- Tags applied via `tags=` in each `@mcp.tool` decorator\\n- Regression: all tools still work without tags; tags are metadata only\\n- Documented in server.py or README so parent server authors know the tag taxonomy\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add `tags=` to all @mcp.tool decorators\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a parent MCP server composing backlog_core, I need backlog_core tools tagged with semantic categories so I can expose only read-only or non-destructive subsets to specific clients using FastMCP's tag filtering.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add tag-based categorization to backlog_core tools for runtime filtering** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fastmcp-creator skill review of backlog_core/server.py\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"20b2ed6ee761d35ce9c9776e1e35ab5ca902c8abe21c44b93d7fcc566e7804d5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTCdoA\"}"}